                <pb facs="co_d27-1" n="1" xml:id="co_d27-1"/>

                <head>CO–27. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>President Alberto Lleras Camargo of Colombia made an official visit to the United
                    States in April 1940. He spent the period April 5–8 in Washington participating
                    in official discussions with President Eisenhower and other United States
                    officials. Thereafter, he traveled through parts of the United States, ending
                    the official phase of his visit on April 14. After spending three days in Miami
                    Beach, Florida, he departed for Colombia on April 17. Documentation relating to
                    preparations for President Lleras Camargo’s visit, including briefing materials
                    and position papers, are in Department of State decimal file 721.11, and the
                    following Department of State lot files: ARA/WST Files, Lot 63 D 20; Conference
                    Files, Lot 64 D 559, CF 1621–1622. For additional documentation, see Department
                    of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, November 16, 1959, p. 718.</p>
            </div>
